          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-44382",
          ":question/problem": "A line $l$ is parallel to $4x-y=22.$  A possible equation for $l$ is",
          ":question/worked-solution": "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of the line $4x-y=22,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-y & =22 \\\\ -y & =-4x+22 \\\\ y & =4x-22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $4.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only line that has a slope of $4$ is $y=4x+8.$"
